title: MikroTik REST API: WireGuard Peers
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 WireGuard peers of a MikroTik router ({/interface/wireguard/peers}).
 Private and preshared keys are not collected.

 A peer with endpoint address and persistent keepalive that is not a
 responder counts as site-to-site: its handshake is renewed about every
 2 minutes, so the time since the last handshake has levels (default
 WARN 5 min, CRIT 15 min, CRIT if there was no handshake yet). All other
 peers count as dial-in (road warriors) without levels by default.
 Also shown: current endpoint, traffic in/out, configured endpoint,
 allowed addresses, keepalive and public key. Levels via the rule
 {MikroTik REST API: WireGuard peers}.

 Special agent {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup >
 Agents > Other integrations, module "WireGuard peers".

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.1.0 by Klaus Paulitsch.

item:
 Interface name and comment of the peer (or its name, or the first 8 characters of the public key).

perfdata:
 Time since the last handshake, traffic in/out.

inventory:
 One service per peer that is not disabled.
